A||||4||Eric||Eric's Fiero Saves the Day||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||05-07-2001||06:26 PM||||There was another central Ohio div. SCCA autocross event this past Sunday.  Unfortunatly, I was substantially outnumbered by MR2s.  And even though a few beat me, I feel as if I represented the Fiero community quite well in my lightly modded 88GT on street tires.<P>Taijiguy showed up, without the intention of racing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> , in his carbureted GT.  His car is pretty cool.  To get to see it in a "soon to be completed state" was a neat opportunity.  He has some big plans, some of which include autocrossing when he gets new motor mounts.<P>I got a crispy burn from being in the sun too long, but that's all part of the autocross experience.  There's a good group of people who comprise the club.  Everyone is really eager to help.  This Sunday was the driver's school, where an experienced driver teaches a group of four to five people the things he or she has learned about driving.  An MR2 guy, believe it or not, was my instructor.  I already knew him and raced against him when I was in C stock, but he still taught me a thing or two even about my car.  When he got a chance to drive it, he was impressed with the Fiero's ability to "rotate".  He drove my car well, but not quite as fast as I did.  Given my moderate amount of autocross experience and copious seat time, that was to be expected.  But, needless to say, I was humbled.  <P>In my lesson group was me, my dad, a guy who had just purchased a 88 MR2 and was just learning how to drive a stick, and a guy with a '01 MR2 spyder.  My dad got lost on his first time out, went through some cones, and tried to run over some people.  He recovered, and was able to pull together a couple good, solid laps.  He doesn't drive my car much, but when he does, I get the feeling he thrashes it by the way he looked out there.  The guy just learning to drive his car was aided a lot by getting the seat time with someone who was familiar with his car.  He started running consistantly, but by no means fast.  And the new MR2 was very quick around the course.  At his fastest, he was probably less than a second slower than me if he didn't beat me outright (I haven't seen the results yet).<P>I'm hooked on racing again.  I'm proud that I didn't kill a single cone too.  Hopefully Chadman will spend some quality time with the Mrs. so he can come out to the next event two weeks away on the 20th.  I was kind of half expecting Roger to show up yesterday also.  I can't wait to see him tear up his Ferrari  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>88GT lowered, kybs, and poly bushings||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||05-07-2001||08:34 PM||||Provided all things go well, and as planned, I should have the mounts in by then, and hopefully my vent baffles will be installed, and the fine tuning on my carb will be completed. (I'm talking some serious tricky stuff, the idle and off-idle circuits can make or break an autocross car) I should have the front end inspected and new bushings and alignment by then. I'll have to run on my Dunlops for now, but what the hell, they're fairly sticky. <BR>Glad we got to meet, and that you had fun and managed to get some more seat time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||05-07-2001||10:59 PM||||I got beat pretty good by a few MR2's and Miatas last time out. I have a stock 87 GT with a junkyard 86 4 speed on street tires. I did manage to edge out the Dodge Dakota by 2 sec tho!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000003||ChadMan||05-08-2001||09:01 AM||||We'll see...I'd like to install the steering-rack bushing I bought from Rodney Dickman before I race again.  But congratulations on running strong!  Who was your instructor?  Phil the MR2 Guy?||||reg||1
